            "target_entity_instance": "quasi-Lagrangian (airmass-following) trajectory",
            "target_entity_type": "SimulationType",
            "paragraph": "This study employs an LES model that explicitly predicts the mass and number of accumulation mode aerosols 44 to simulate SCT along an airmass-following trajectory, which is based on a composite of summertime conditions over the Northeast Pacific Ocean 45. This SCT case study has been used to identify mechanisms underlying marine low cloud responses to warming and increased CO2 46 and the aerosol-mediated, precipitation-induced breakup of stratocumulus clouds along the transition 47. In this study, the interplay between cloud responses to greenhouse- induced warming and cloud-aerosol interactions is explored in simulations of subtropical marine low clouds in an airmass that moves over progressively warmer sea surface temperatures, following the setup of a previous study (Bretherton & Blossey, 2014), henceforth BB2014, but including a prognostic treatment of aerosol number and mass concentrations.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
